You are building UI for AgentStatus by Carmel Labs. Follow these rules on every single response, no exceptions.

FONTS
- Primary font: Plus Jakarta Sans (always import from Google Fonts)
- Secondary font: DM Sans (for specific UI components only)
- Never use any other font

COLORS
- Never hardcode hex values
- Never use Tailwind color classes like bg-blue-500 or text-gray-700
- Always use hsl(var(--token-name)) for every color value
- The only colors that exist are the ones defined in the design system below

DESIGN TOKENS (light mode)
--background: 0 0% 100%
--foreground: 222.2 84% 4.9%
--card: 0 0% 100%
--card-foreground: 222.2 84% 4.9%
--primary: 221.2 83.2% 53.3%
--primary-foreground: 210 40% 98%
--secondary: 210 40% 96%
--secondary-foreground: 222.2 84% 4.9%
--muted: 210 40% 96%
--muted-foreground: 215.4 16.3% 46.9%
--accent: 210 40% 96%
--accent-foreground: 222.2 84% 4.9%
--destructive: 0 84.2% 60.2%
--destructive-foreground: 210 40% 98%
--border: 214.3 31.8% 91.4%
--input: 214.3 31.8% 91.4%
--ring: 221.2 83.2% 53.3%
--radius: 0.5rem
--brand-navy: 214 39% 17%

BRAND ACCENT COLORS (use sparingly, for highlights and logo elements only)
- Logo orange: #f97316
- Hero yellow highlight: #facc15

BUTTONS
- Primary CTA: background hsl(var(--primary)), text hsl(var(--primary-foreground))
- Never invent other color combinations for buttons

BORDER RADIUS
- Always use var(--radius) which equals 0.5rem
- Exception: Fabric product theme uses 1.5rem

GENERAL RULES
- If you are unsure about a color, font, or spacing value, ask before inventing one
- Never use Tailwind default colors
- Always match the clean, professional aesthetic of agentstatus.dev
BACKGROUNDS
- Never use background images, textures, watercolor effects, or decorative patterns
- Backgrounds are always flat colors using hsl(var(--token)) only
- The only gradients allowed are ones explicitly asked for by the user